# tests/mpx4-ready's run list for QEMU's user-mode network (px24): the
# lines of user/mpx4-ready.run that cross the wire, with tools/ready-host
# at this host's end of the two forwarded ports (ordinary sockets), and
# one probe first. Each is a line of that list, held to Linux's output
# for it.
/bin/nbprobe
/bin/epollecho 7 10.0.2.2 9711
/bin/waitwolf serve 7101 12 1 10.0.2.2 9712
/bin/waitwolf call 10.0.2.2 9713 12 1 3
